#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:1
msgid "Release 2.26.0 (2025-01-22)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:3
msgid ""
"Support for relative path inputs [\\#10089](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/10089)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:5
msgid ""
"Flakes can now refer to other flakes in the same repository using relative "
"paths, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:6
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.foo.url = \"path:./foo\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:9
msgid ""
"uses the flake in the `foo` subdirectory of the referring flake. For more "
"information, see the documentation on [the `path` flake input type](../"
"command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md#path-fetcher)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:11
msgid ""
"This feature required a change to the lock file format. Previous Nix "
"versions will not be able to use lock files that have locks for relative "
"path inputs in them."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:13
msgid ""
"Flake lock file generation now ignores local registries [\\#12019](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12019)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:15
msgid ""
"When resolving indirect flake references like `nixpkgs` in `flake.nix` "
"files, Nix will no longer use the system and user flake registries. It will "
"only use the global flake registry and overrides given on the command line "
"via `--override-flake`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:17
msgid ""
"This avoids accidents where users have local registry overrides that map "
"`nixpkgs` to a `path:` flake in the local file system, which then end up in "
"committed lock files pushed to other users."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:19
msgid ""
"In the future, we may remove the use of the registry during lock file "
"generation altogether. It's better to explicitly specify the URL of a flake "
"input. For example, instead of"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:25
msgid "write"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:26
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{\n"
"  inputs.nixpkgs.url = \"github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-24.11\";\n"
"  outputs = { self, nixpkgs }: { ... };\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:33
msgid ""
"`nix copy` supports `--profile` and `--out-link` [\\#11657](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/pull/11657)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:35
msgid ""
"The `nix copy` command now has flags `--profile` and `--out-link`, similar "
"to `nix build`. `--profile` makes a profile point to the top-level store "
"path, while `--out-link` create symlinks to the top-level store paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:38
msgid ""
"For example, when updating the local NixOS system profile from a NixOS "
"system closure on a remote machine, instead of"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:39
msgid ""
"```\n"
"# nix copy --from ssh://server $path\n"
"# nix build --profile /nix/var/nix/profiles/system $path\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:43
msgid "you can now do"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:44
msgid ""
"```\n"
"# nix copy --from ssh://server --profile /nix/var/nix/profiles/system $path\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:47
msgid ""
"The advantage is that this avoids a time window where _path_ is not a "
"garbage collector root, and so could be deleted by a concurrent `nix store "
"gc` process."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:49
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate --eval` now supports `--raw` [\\#12119](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/12119)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:51
msgid ""
"The `nix-instantiate --eval` command now supports a `--raw` flag, when used "
"the evaluation result must be a string, which is printed verbatim without "
"quotation marks or escaping."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:55
msgid ""
"Improved `NIX_SSHOPTS` parsing for better SSH option handling [\\#5181]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/5181) [\\#12020](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/12020)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:57
msgid ""
"The parsing of the `NIX_SSHOPTS` environment variable has been improved to "
"handle spaces and quotes correctly. Previously, incorrectly split SSH "
"options could cause failures in commands like `nix-copy-closure`, especially "
"when using complex SSH invocations such as `-o ProxyCommand=\"ssh -W %h:"
"%p ...\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:61
msgid ""
"This change introduces a `shellSplitString` function to ensure that "
"`NIX_SSHOPTS` is parsed in a manner consistent with shell behavior, "
"addressing common parsing errors."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:65
msgid "For example, the following now works as expected:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:68
msgid "'-o ProxyCommand=\"ssh -W %h:%p ...\"'"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:71
msgid ""
"This update improves the reliability of SSH-related operations using "
"`NIX_SSHOPTS` across Nix CLIs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:73
msgid "Nix is now built using Meson"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:75
msgid ""
"As proposed in [RFC 132](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/pull/132), Nix's "
"build system now uses Meson/Ninja. The old Make-based build system has been "
"removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.26.md:77
msgid ""
"Evaluation caching now works for dirty Git workdirs [\\#11992](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11992)"
msgstr ""

